WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.720
Daenerys Targaryen has been on quite a journey
throughout Game of Thrones, and it's anyone's

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.100
guess where she winds up at the end of Season
8.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.080
Some of those guesses, though, sound more
plausible than others.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.200
Here's a look at some Daenerys fan theories
that just might come true.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.540
"I'ma show you something real special.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.900
The script of the final season of Game of
Thrones, mmm!"

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.660
Perhaps the most complex theory about Daenerys
is that she will not only die, but will actually

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.900
become a White Walker - and it will be Jon
Snow that kills her.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.800
This theory hinges on the legend of the ancient
warrior Azor Ahai, who has been prophesied

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.520
to return one day to save the world.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.180
In author George R.R. Martin's Song of Fire
and Ice book series, which the show is based

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:45.410
on, it's said that Azor Ahai forged his famous
flaming sword Lightbringer by plunging it

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.820
into the heart of his beloved wife, Nissa
Nissa.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:53.000
Some fans think that Jon is Azor Ahai reborn,
and that to reforge Lightbringer, he will

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.110
need to kill Dany.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.360
"in the ancient books it's written that a
warrior will draw a burning sword from the

00:00:59.360 --> 00:00:59.860
fire.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.480
And that sword shall be Lightbringer!"

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:07.360
Making this theory even more complicated is
the idea that Dany will then rise as a White

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.580
Walker, just as her dragon previously rose
from the dead.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.200
This is based on another ancient legend from
the book about a long ago Commander of the

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.860
Night's Watch who married a "corpse bride."

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.980
Some fans think that these two legends are
actually one and the same, and that Nissa

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.420
Nissa was the corpse bride.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:28.180
So if Jon is Azor Ahai reborn, weilding a
sword of fire, and Daenerys is Nissa Nissa

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:32.299
reborn, reigning as a White Walker, the two
together will make up the "song of ice and

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.640
fire" that gives the book series its title.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.400
Hey, we told you it was complex!

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:41.340
Speaking of prophecies from the book, there's
another one that didn't make it into the show

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.820
but still could prove crucial.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:47.900
At one point, Daenerys is told she will be
betrayed three times - once for gold, once

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.420
for blood, and once for love.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:53.140
Two of these have already happened in the
show: Ser Jorah Mormont betrayed her to King

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.760
Robert for gold, while the witch Mirri Maz
Duur betrayed her for blood.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.120
So some fans theorize that it will be Tyrion
who betrays her for love.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.900
Some say for love of his family, others suggest
for his own unrequited love of Daenerys.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.640
Say it ain't so, Tyrion!

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.560
So, back to that whole Azor Ahai thing.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.280
Many characters in the series believe Azor
Ahai is the subject of another prophecy called

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:18.790
"the prince that was promised," which foretells
the rebirth of an ancient hero who will save

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:19.360
the world.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.120
Melisandre, the Red Preistess, is a big fan
of assuming any random schmoe is the Prince

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.180
that was Promised, first declaring it to be
Stannis, and later assuming it's actually

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.040
Jon Snow.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:33.800
But one theory originally espoused in the
books by the Night's Watch Maester Aemon Targaryen

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.080
is the idea that Daenerys is actually the
prophesied hero.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:41.231
It turns out the original prophecy was in
the ancient language High Valyrian, which

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:46.320
is genderless - meaning it could actually
refer to a princess just as easily as a prince.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.959
One of the most explosive revelations of Thrones'
seventh season was the reveal that Jon Snow's

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:57.489
name isn't Jon Snow at all it's Aegon Targaryen,
and he's not Ned Stark's lowborn bastard,

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:00.350
but a member of the most royal family in all
of Westeros.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:05.460
Born to Ned's sister Lyanna Stark, the man
audiences know as Jon Snow is the son of Rhaegar

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:09.660
Targaryen, making him the rightful heir to
the Iron Throne and Daenerys' nephew.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.200
"Jon isn't really my father's son.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.060
He's the son of Rhaegar Targaryen and my aunt,
Lyanna Stark."

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:22.180
Some fans expect this to be a major point
of contention, even leading to Jon and Daenerys

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.960
battling each other for the Iron Throne.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.560
Let's hope it doesn't come to that!

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.500
Ever since audiences met Daenerys Targaryen,
they've been prepared to accept her as one

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.510
of the show's heroes.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.680
But what if she's actually the ultimate villain?

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.700
There's precedent, of course, as the whole
reason her family was deposed in the first

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:42.050
place is because the Mad King Aerys went on
a literal reign of terror, burning people

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:46.000
alive at the slightest whim - just as Dany
began doing in Season 7.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.900
In particular, the Mad King threatened to
destroy all of King's Landing.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:53.620
That's something Daenerys seems poised to
do before the series end, though she won't

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.160
need wildfire to do it.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:59.950
A confrontation with arch-enemy Cersei Lannister,
who currently sits on the Iron Throne, seems

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:00.780
inevitable.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:05.280
And since leaked set photos seem to show King's
Landing in a state of destruction, it looks

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.940
as though Dany and her dragons may finally
finish what the Mad King promised.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.220
Whether or not she completes her heel turn
in the process to become a true despot remains

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:13.860
to be seen.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:19.080
Daenerys's journey began with a political
marriage, and some fans theorize her journey

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.240
will end the same way.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:24.919
In order to solidify her claim to the Iron
Throne, a political marriage to Jon snow - or

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.100
even Jaime Lannister! - makes some sense.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:32.189
Still, some sentimental fans theorize that
Dany will actually marry Ser Jorah... before

00:04:32.189 --> 00:04:35.640
he's forced to kill her, and then die himself
trying to stop the Night King.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.140
Okay, maybe they aren't so sentimental.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:42.580
This is just one of several fan theories that
also believe Daenerys will become pregnant

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.619
with Jon's child, and that the series will
end with their offspring set to inherit the

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:47.280
Iron Throne.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.100
Hey, at least somebody in that scenario would
have a happy ending...

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.240
...unlike our final fan theory, which suggests
that Dany might actually die at the beginning

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:58.540
of the season and will never even have a chance
to do any of that stuff.

00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:03.080
Eagle-eyed fans compiling reports from the
various filming locations around the globe

00:05:03.089 --> 00:05:07.650
reported that while nearly every single other
character of note appeared for filming, Emilia

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:12.219
Clarke, who plays Daenerys, did not, leading
some to conclude that her character must die

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.560
early, before those locations come into play.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.260
Hey, you know what they say:

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:17.920
"Valor morghulis."

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:20.500
"Valor morghulis."

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.580
"Valor marghuils."

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.600
"Yes, all men must die.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:28.740
But we are not men."

